From: V3 Gold <v3gold@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 02:21:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] V3 Gold: experimental motion blur removal and 60 FPS
 switches

Persona 4 Golden draws what it rendered in the previous frame back over
the new frame, partly transparent: its motion blur. The Vulkan renderer
now notices full-screen draws (6 vertices or fewer) that sample render
targets and reports them to the in-game menu (renderer/gold_lab.h,
android/jni/gold_lab.cpp). With the fix on, a draw that samples a
full-size render target drawn one or two frames before:
- is skipped if it alpha-blends that single image over the screen,
- or gets the new frame bound in its place if it also samples the new
  frame (a shader mixing the two).
Sampled render targets are remembered per texture slot (texture.cpp)
and looked up in the surface cache at draw time for their age.

JNI for the 60 FPS experiment: Vita3K's FPS hack switched live, the
game's frame rate, a search of the game's executable for a 32-bit value,
reads and writes of single words, and Vita3K's patch folder and the
running title ID.

Emulator tells GoldLab when a game starts and stops, so the saved
switches apply at every start.
